		<item>
		<title>Bajaj Finserv, Aviso Specialty, Swiss Re CorSo, Everest, Lockton: 13 APAC insurance people moves of the week</title>
		<link>https://insuranceasianews.com/bajaj-finserv-everest-aviso-lockton-swiss-re-corso-13-apac-insurance-people-moves-of-the-week/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Roshan Nambiar]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 09:00:56 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid isPermaLink="false">https://insuranceasianews.com/?p=230635</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Mitsui Bussan Pana Harrison, Marsh, Axa XL, Great Eastern, HDI Global, Knightcorp, Ace Insurance Brokers and Howden Re also made personnel changes over the last week.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://insuranceasianews.com/bajaj-finserv-everest-aviso-lockton-swiss-re-corso-13-apac-insurance-people-moves-of-the-week/">Bajaj Finserv, Aviso Specialty, Swiss Re CorSo, Everest, Lockton: 13 APAC insurance people moves of the week</a> appeared first on <a href="https://insuranceasianews.com">InsuranceAsia News</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>InsuranceAsia News wraps up the people moves from the insurance industry in Asia this week.</p>
<h2 class="news-title">1. Bajaj Finserv picks ex-GIC chairman to lead reinsurance foray</h2>
<p>Indian financial services group <strong>Bajaj Finserv</strong> has chosen former GIC Re chairman and managing director <strong>Ramaswamy Narayanan</strong> to lead its entry into the reinsurance sector.</p>
<p>Narayanan, an industry veteran with over three decades of experience, will lead Bajaj Finserv’s new reinsurance division. He is due to join the firm next week.</p>
<p>He retired as GIC Re’s chairman and managing director in September after almost three years in charge.</p>
<p><span style="letter-spacing: 0px;">Read the full story</span><span style="letter-spacing: 0px;"> <a href="https://insuranceasianews.com/bajaj-finserv-picks-ex-gic-chairman-ramaswamy-narayanan-to-lead-reinsurance-foray-report/">here</a>.</span></p>
<h2 class="news-title">2. Aviso Specialty hires Marsh veteran to stand up capital solutions group</h2>
<p>Australian specialty broker <strong>Aviso Specialty</strong> has appointed <strong>Eric Wojcik</strong> as head of capital and guarantee solutions, effective March 2027.</p>
<p>With the appointment, the broker will establish a new capital solutions group, which is designed to bring together specialist expertise from across the business to support clients where risk, capital and commercial considerations intersect.</p>
<p><span style="letter-spacing: 0px;">Read the full story <a href="https://insuranceasianews.com/aviso-specialty-hires-marsh-veteran-eric-wojcik-to-stand-up-capital-solutions-group/">here</a>.</span></p>
<h2 class="news-title"><img decoding="async" class="size-thumbnail wp-image-230646 alignleft" src="https://insuranceasianews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Adnan-A.-Bhat-150x150.png" alt="" width="150" height="150" srcset="https://insuranceasianews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Adnan-A.-Bhat-150x150.png 150w, https://insuranceasianews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Adnan-A.-Bhat-300x300.png 300w, https://insuranceasianews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Adnan-A.-Bhat-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://insuranceasianews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Adnan-A.-Bhat-768x767.png 768w, https://insuranceasianews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Adnan-A.-Bhat.png 1043w" sizes="(max-width: 991px) 100vw, (max-width: 1549px) 65vw, 984px" />3. Swiss Re CorSo hires APAC global network manager</h2>
<p class="news-title"><strong>Adnan Bhat</strong> has joined <strong>Swiss Re Corporate Solutions (Swiss Re CorSo)</strong> as global network manager for Asia Pacific within its international programs team, effective from October 5.</p>
<p>Bhat has joined Swiss Re CorSo as a vice president responsible for supporting the growth of the commercial insurer’s partner ecosystem across APAC.</p>
<p><span style="letter-spacing: 0px;">Read the full story</span> <a style="letter-spacing: 0px;" href="https://insuranceasianews.com/adnan-bhat-joins-swiss-re-corso-as-apac-global-network-manager/">here.</a></p>
<h2 class="news-title">4. Everest names APAC financial lines director for wholesale, specialty</h2>
<p><strong><span class="ckyfpw ckymt4"><span class="ckymt4" data-sdui-anchor-id="commentary-SUtVOUCKVxr2ctjSwtQ3Q7D_LQAlD6fxghyduiL69HI-acf8986e-ac30-46ee-b314-74a04f3be69d::109">Everest</span></span></strong> has appointed <strong>Adrian Di Pasquale</strong> as financial lines director for wholesale and specialty in Asia Pacific.</p>
<p>Singapore-based Di Pasquale joins from Chubb, where he had served as Southeast Asia financial lines underwriting manager since April 2025.</p>
<p><span style="letter-spacing: 0px;">Read the full story</span> <a style="letter-spacing: 0px;" href="https://insuranceasianews.com/everest-names-adrian-di-pasquale-as-apac-financial-lines-director-for-wholesale-specialty/">here.</a></p>
<h2 class="news-title">5. Lockton taps Price Forbes director as senior consultant for Japan business</h2>
<p><strong>Lockton</strong> has appointed <strong>Kenichiro Miki</strong> as a senior consultant for its Japan business in its Singapore regional office.</p>
<p>Before joining Lockton, Miki worked as an executive director at Price Forbes in Singapore, where he was head of the wholesale broker’s Japan practice from April 2025.</p>
<p><span style="letter-spacing: 0px;">Read the full story</span> <a style="letter-spacing: 0px;" href="https://insuranceasianews.com/lockton-taps-kenichiro-miki-as-senior-consultant-for-japan-business/">here.</a></p>
<h2 class="news-title">6. Mitsui Bussan Pana Harrison appoints head of general insurance <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright size-thumbnail wp-image-230647" src="https://insuranceasianews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Alice-Lim-150x150.png" alt="" width="150" height="150" srcset="https://insuranceasianews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Alice-Lim-150x150.png 150w, https://insuranceasianews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Alice-Lim-300x300.png 300w, https://insuranceasianews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Alice-Lim-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://insuranceasianews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Alice-Lim-768x767.png 768w, https://insuranceasianews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Alice-Lim.png 1043w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 991px) 100vw, (max-width: 1549px) 65vw, 984px" /></h2>
<p><strong>Mitsui Bussan Pana Harrison</strong>, the Lloyd’s (re)insurance broker majority-owned by Mitsui, has appointed<strong> Alice Lim</strong> as head of general insurance.</p>
<p>In her new role, Alice will lead the firm&#8217;s general insurance and employee benefits and work closely with it&#8217;s team and business partners to support the continued development of its portfolio.</p>
<p><span style="letter-spacing: 0px;">Read the full story</span><span style="letter-spacing: 0px;"> <a href="https://insuranceasianews.com/mitsui-bussan-pana-harrison-appoints-alice-lim-as-head-of-general-insurance/">here</a>.</span></p>
<h2 class="news-title">7. Marsh reshuffles Australia, Thailand teams</h2>
<p><span class=""><strong>Marsh</strong> has appointed </span><strong><span class="">Sonya Febbo</span></strong><span class=""> as head of authorised representatives for corporate and commercial in Australia. </span></p>
<p>Melbourne-based Febbo previously spent over 15 years as managing director of XS Insurance, a corporate authorised representative of Marsh.</p>
<p><strong>Jack Petrie</strong> has relocated from Melbourne to Bangkok to take up the role as cyber practice leader for Marsh Thailand.</p>
<p>Petrie spent the last three years as managing principal for Marsh in Melbourne, having joined from the Victorian Managed Insurance Authority in October 2023.</p>
<p><span style="letter-spacing: 0px;">Read the full story <a href="https://insuranceasianews.com/marsh-elevates-sonya-febbo-to-australia-head-of-authorised-representatives/">here</a> and <a href="https://insuranceasianews.com/jack-petrie-shifts-to-thailand-to-head-marsh-asias-cyber-practice/">here</a>.</span></p>
<h2 class="news-title">8. Axa XL promotes senior underwriter to Asia underwriting manager for political risk, credit, bond</h2>
<p><strong>Axa XL</strong> has promoted <strong>Paul Gardner</strong> to underwriting manager for political risk, credit and bond (PRCB) in Asia.</p>
<p>Based in Singapore, Gardner brings over 35 years of experience in structured finance and cross-border solutions, with a career spanning project finance, commodity finance, tax, leasing, export credit agencies, as well as advisory and workout solutions, according to the post.</p>
<p><span style="letter-spacing: 0px;">Read the full story</span><span style="letter-spacing: 0px;"> <a href="https://insuranceasianews.com/axa-xl-promotes-paul-gardner-to-asia-underwriting-manager-for-political-risk-credit-bond/">here</a>.</span></p>
<h2 class="news-title">9. HDI Global Japan names general manager of distribution and marketing</h2>
<p><strong>HDI Global</strong> has appointed <strong>Kei Kimura</strong> as general manager of distribution and marketing at its Japan branch.</p>
<p>Kimura stepped into the role on October 1 with leadership experience and a track record of driving business growth, developing high-performing teams, and building client partnerships.</p>
<p><span style="letter-spacing: 0px;">Read the full story</span><span style="letter-spacing: 0px;"> <a href="https://insuranceasianews.com/hdi-global-japan-names-kei-kimura-as-general-manager-of-distribution-and-marketing/">here</a>.</span></p>
<h2 class="news-title"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-thumbnail wp-image-230648 alignleft" src="https://insuranceasianews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Daniel-Rombach-150x150.png" alt="" width="150" height="150" srcset="https://insuranceasianews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Daniel-Rombach-150x150.png 150w, https://insuranceasianews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Daniel-Rombach-300x300.png 300w, https://insuranceasianews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Daniel-Rombach-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://insuranceasianews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Daniel-Rombach-768x767.png 768w, https://insuranceasianews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Daniel-Rombach.png 1043w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 991px) 100vw, (max-width: 1549px) 65vw, 984px" />10. Great Eastern appoints VP for digital distribution platforms</h2>
<p><strong>Daniel Rombach</strong> has joined <strong>Great Eastern Insurance</strong> as vice president for digital distribution platforms.</p>
<p>Rombach, who began the role in September, moved from Chubb, where he was most recently the accident and health product owner for Asia Pacific since relocating to Singapore in April 2024.</p>
<p><span style="letter-spacing: 0px;">Read the full story</span> <a style="letter-spacing: 0px;" href="https://insuranceasianews.com/daniel-rombach-joins-great-eastern-as-vp-for-digital-distribution-platforms/">here.</a></p>
<h2 class="news-title">11. Australian broker Knightcorp adds financial lines account director</h2>
<p>Australian broker <strong>Knightcorp</strong> has appointed <strong>Justin Geldart</strong> as account director for financial lines.</p>
<p>Perth-based Geldart joins the broker with nearly three decades of insurance experience, last holding the position of client manager at Gallagher since January 2024.</p>
<p><span style="letter-spacing: 0px;">Read the full story</span> <a style="letter-spacing: 0px;" href="https://insuranceasianews.com/australian-broker-knightcorp-adds-justin-geldart-as-financial-lines-account-director/">here.</a></p>
<h2 class="news-title">12. Ace Insurance Brokers hires senior vice president</h2>
<p><strong>Ace Insurance Brokers</strong> has tapped <strong>Shashin Kowshik</strong> as a senior vice president in its Bengaluru office.</p>
<p>Kowshik joined Ace Insurance Brokers after more than a decade at Aon, having held various underwriting roles at Bajaj Allianz General Insurance for almost 10 years earlier prior to that.</p>
<p><span style="letter-spacing: 0px;">Read the full story</span> <a style="letter-spacing: 0px;" href="https://insuranceasianews.com/ace-insurance-brokers-hires-shashin-kowshik-as-senior-vice-president/">here.</a></p>
<h2 class="news-title"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="alignright size-thumbnail wp-image-230649" src="https://insuranceasianews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Titus-Wu-150x150.png" alt="" width="150" height="150" srcset="https://insuranceasianews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Titus-Wu-150x150.png 150w, https://insuranceasianews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Titus-Wu-300x300.png 300w, https://insuranceasianews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Titus-Wu-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://insuranceasianews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Titus-Wu-768x767.png 768w, https://insuranceasianews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Titus-Wu.png 1043w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 991px) 100vw, (max-width: 1549px) 65vw, 984px" />13. Howden Re names associate director for APAC facultative</h2>
<p><strong>Howden Re</strong> has appointed <strong>Titus Wu</strong> as associate director for facultative in APAC, based in Singapore.</p>
<p>Wu relocated to Singapore from Hong Kong for the new role, having most recently been an associate director for reinsurance with Aon in Hong Kong, where he worked for five years.</p>
<p><span style="letter-spacing: 0px;">Read the full story</span> <a style="letter-spacing: 0px;" href="https://insuranceasianews.com/howden-re-hires-titus-wu-as-associate-director-for-apac-facultative/">here.</a></p>
<h2>Other moves you may have missed</h2>
<p><strong>Specialty MGA</strong>, part of MNK Group, <a href="https://insuranceasianews.com/specialty-mga-hires-david-higgins-to-lead-global-bloodstock-expansion/">has appointed <strong>David Higgins</strong></a> to lead the expansion of its global bloodstock portfolio, including into the Australasia region. As a senior underwriter with more than 40 years of underwriting experience across bloodstock and aviation, London-based Higgins (pictured) will focus on building a bloodstock portfolio comprising major-value risks worldwide in his new role.</p>
<p>Ex-Lloyd’s CEO <a href="https://insuranceasianews.com/ex-lloyds-chief-john-neal-joins-software-developer-lusyi/"><strong>John Neal</strong> has joined software developer LUSYi</a> as a non-executive chairman. He returns to the industry after a hiatus, following a tumultuous period that saw planned moves to Aon and AIG unravel amid a Lloyd&#8217;s investigation.</p>
<p><em>For more InsuranceAsia News (IAN) people moves at brokers, insurers, reinsurers, insurtechs, specialty players, MGAs and loss adjusters across Asia Pacific’s fast-growing (re)insurance markets click <a href="https://insuranceasianews.com/post_category/people/">here</a>.</em></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://insuranceasianews.com/bajaj-finserv-everest-aviso-lockton-swiss-re-corso-13-apac-insurance-people-moves-of-the-week/">Bajaj Finserv, Aviso Specialty, Swiss Re CorSo, Everest, Lockton: 13 APAC insurance people moves of the week</a> appeared first on <a href="https://insuranceasianews.com">InsuranceAsia News</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
			</item>
